{"id":5235,"date":"2019-01-01T13:59:03","date_gmt":"2019-01-01T18:59:03","guid":{"rendered":"https:\/\/herbnkathy.com\/?p=5235"},"modified":"2019-01-01T13:59:10","modified_gmt":"2019-01-01T18:59:10","slug":"another-great-climb-er-drive-up-the-mountain","status":"publish","type":"post","link":"https:\/\/herbnkathy.com\/2019\/01\/01\/another-great-climb-er-drive-up-the-mountain\/","title":{"rendered":"Another Great  Climb .. er, Drive up the Mountain"},"content":{"rendered":"\n<p>We met Rob &amp; Michelle when we were working up in Michigan last summer at <a href=\"https:\/\/www.peremarquettervpark.com\/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noreferrer noopener\" aria-label=\"Pere Marquette Oaks RV Park (opens in a new tab)\">Pere Marquette Oaks RV Park<\/a>.  They were pretty new to the full-time RV lifestyle themselves having retired from work, selling their home and buying the truck and the 5th wheel to live in as they traveled the country.<\/p>\n\n\n\n<figure class=\"wp-block-image\"><img loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"760\" height=\"428\" src=\"https:\/\/i2.wp.com\/herbnkathy.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/2018\/12\/20181211_105535.jpg?fit=700%2C394&amp;ssl=1\" alt=\"\" class=\"wp-image-5237\" srcset=\"https:\/\/herbnkathy.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/2018\/12\/20181211_105535.jpg 760w, https:\/\/herbnkathy.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/2018\/12\/20181211_105535-300x169.jpg 300w, https:\/\/herbnkathy.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/2018\/12\/20181211_105535-768x432.jpg 768w, https:\/\/herbnkathy.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/2018\/12\/20181211_105535-1024x576.jpg 1024w\" sizes=\"auto, (max-width: 760px) 100vw, 760px\" \/><\/figure>\n\n\n\n<p>We were glad to find that Rob &amp; Michelle had made their way from Michigan to Arizona and were staying at an RV park near Tucson for the month of December.<\/p>\n\n\n\n<p>We reached out to them through Facebook and then spent the day together driving up to Mt. Lemmon (about 9000&#8242;).  It was a beautiful day with temps down in Tucson at about 70+ degrees and the sun was shining brightly.  We knew the temperature up on the mountain would be 20-30 degrees cooler.<\/p>\n\n\n\n<p>Mt. Lemmon has a summit at 9159&#8242; and is located in the Santa Catalina Mountain Range of the Coronado National Forest.  The Catalina Highway is a two lane paved road that heads north from Tucson and winds it&#8217;s way on up to Mt. Lemmon Ski Valley and the little town of Summerhaven that sports a couple restaurants, a general store, and a few other small businesses.  <\/p>\n\n\n\n<figure class=\"wp-block-image\"><img loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"627\" height=\"540\" src=\"https:\/\/herbnkathy.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/2018\/12\/Map-Mt-Lemmon.jpg\" alt=\"\" class=\"wp-image-5238\" srcset=\"https:\/\/herbnkathy.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/2018\/12\/Map-Mt-Lemmon.jpg 627w, https:\/\/herbnkathy.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/2018\/12\/Map-Mt-Lemmon-300x259.jpg 300w, https:\/\/herbnkathy.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/2018\/12\/Map-Mt-Lemmon-768x662.jpg 768w\" sizes=\"auto, (max-width: 627px) 100vw, 627px\" \/><figcaption>The white squiggly line you see going up from Tanque Verde is the Catalina Highway that takes you to the summit<\/figcaption><\/figure>\n\n\n\n<p><a href=\"https:\/\/www.mtlemmon.com\/summerhaven\/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noreferrer noopener\" aria-label=\"Summerhaven (opens in a new tab)\">Summerhaven<\/a>, although home to a few full-time residents, is mostly inhabited by folks who come up from the hot desert climate to escape from the heat of the summers.<\/p>\n\n\n\n<figure class=\"wp-block-image\"><img loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"760\" height=\"428\" src=\"https:\/\/i0.wp.com\/herbnkathy.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/2018\/12\/20181211_133653.jpg?fit=700%2C394&amp;ssl=1\" alt=\"\" class=\"wp-image-5236\" srcset=\"https:\/\/herbnkathy.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/2018\/12\/20181211_133653.jpg 760w, https:\/\/herbnkathy.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/2018\/12\/20181211_133653-300x169.jpg 300w, https:\/\/herbnkathy.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/2018\/12\/20181211_133653-768x432.jpg 768w, https:\/\/herbnkathy.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/2018\/12\/20181211_133653-1024x576.jpg 1024w\" sizes=\"auto, (max-width: 760px) 100vw, 760px\" \/><figcaption>One of the restaurants in Summerhaven on Mt. Lemmon<\/figcaption><\/figure>\n\n\n\n<p>We stopped at most every wide spot in the road to be able to get out and marvel at the sites as we looked at the oddly shaped rock formations and the view of the expanse of Tucson down below.<\/p>\n\n\n\n<figure class=\"wp-block-image\"><img loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"1024\" height=\"576\" src=\"https:\/\/herbnkathy.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/2019\/01\/20181211_115107-1024x576.jpg\" alt=\"\" class=\"wp-image-5255\" srcset=\"https:\/\/herbnkathy.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/2019\/01\/20181211_115107-1024x576.jpg 1024w, https:\/\/herbnkathy.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/2019\/01\/20181211_115107-300x169.jpg 300w, https:\/\/herbnkathy.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/2019\/01\/20181211_115107-768x432.jpg 768w, https:\/\/herbnkathy.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/2019\/01\/20181211_115107.jpg 760w\" sizes=\"auto, (max-width: 1024px) 100vw, 1024px\" \/><\/figure>\n\n\n\n<p>Remember, you can click on any of the thumbnails below to see an enlarged view and then you can scroll right or left to see the next picture.<\/p>\n\n\n\n<ul class=\"wp-block-gallery columns-3 is-cropped wp-block-gallery-1 is-layout-flex wp-block-gallery-is-layout-flex\"><li class=\"blocks-gallery-item\"><figure><img loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"760\" height=\"428\" src=\"https:\/\/i2.wp.com\/herbnkathy.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/2019\/01\/20181211_103002-1.jpg?fit=700%2C394&amp;ssl=1\" alt=\"\" data-id=\"5259\" data-link=\"https:\/\/herbnkathy.com\/?attachment_id=5259\" class=\"wp-image-5259\" srcset=\"https:\/\/herbnkathy.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/2019\/01\/20181211_103002-1.jpg 760w, https:\/\/herbnkathy.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/2019\/01\/20181211_103002-1-300x169.